        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Premier Protein powder is a good-value mainstream whey: 30 g of protein for about 150 calories per two-scoop serving, an isolate-led blend and a cost per 25 g that holds its own against the biggest gym brands. Chocolate Milkshake is the one to buy first, Cafe Latte suits morning shakes, and Protein Plus Fiber is worth it if you are short on fiber.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip it if you are a drug-tested athlete, want to avoid artificial sweeteners or need more than three flavors. In those cases a certified whey such as Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard or one of the picks in our whey rankings is the better buy.
